why:
RA gives a chat's door a runs-scoped route, but no tool in an eidolon calls it. An agent today can only start a graph with `eidolon workflow run` through bash, which the stock table allows as "the harness itself" (eidolon/crates/rune/policy.rn:331-333). Such a run gets no chat tag, sits outside the one-browser cap, and lands only in eidolon's own sessions dir (eidolon/crates/cli/src/workflow.rs:1-4).
A plugin tool is how Minerva gives an agent a perch route without editing eidolon. T3 set the pattern, and it is copied here:
- one tool file per verb;
- a byte-identical shared tail: the loopback-only url file, the scoped token file as a Bearer, and one-sentence errors (plugins/term/tools/list.rn:23-128);
- the installer's per-verb trust arm (installer/src/plugins.rs:227-263);
- the bundle's copy of every plugins/*/ folder with a plugin.rn (installer/build.sh:58-88, nix/plugins.nix:14-29), which needs no edit for a new folder.

